1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
The end of an empire...the beginning of a legend.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
The Last Legion is a action, adventure, fantasy film directed by Doug Lefler.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
As the Roman empire crumbles, young Romulus Augustus flees the city and embarks on
a perilous voyage to Britain to track down a legion of supporters.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Aurelius, played by Colin Firth.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Ambrosinus, played by Ben Kingsley.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Mira, played by Aishwarya Rai Bachchan.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Odoacer, played by Peter Mullan.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Wulfila, played by Kevin McKidd.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Nestor, played by John Hannah.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The Last Legion is a 2007 historical action adventure film directed
by Doug Lefler and  produced by Dino De Laurentiis.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It is based on the 2002 novel of the same name by Valerio Massimo Manfredi.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It stars Colin Firth, Ben Kingsley, Aishwarya Rai, Thomas Brodie-Sangster,
Peter Mullan, Kevin McKidd, John Hannah, and Iain Glen.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It premiered in Abu Dhabi on 6 April 2007.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film is loosely inspired by the events of 5th-century European
history, notably the collapse of the Western Roman Empire.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
This is coupled with other facts and legends from the history of Britain and fantastic
elements from the legend of King Arthur to provide a basis for the Arthurian legend.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
The film explores themes of roman empire, sword, emperor, druid, ancient rome.
